{{Nofootnotes}} {{Plane | image = Demonweb Pits - Wayne England.jpg | caption = The Demonweb Pits | name = Demonweb Pits | othernames = Lolth's Web | symbol = Abyss.png | demonym = | natives = [[Spider]]s, [[yochlol]], [[abyssal widow]]s, [[chwidencha]], [[petitioners]] | languages = | basicrefs = <ref name="DD-28">{{Cite book/Demihuman Deities|28}}</ref><ref name="R.M">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback/Map}}</ref> | type-GW = Layer | shape-size-GW = Infinite | gravity-GW = None | time-GW = | morphic-GW = | element-energy-GW = | alignment-GW = [[Chaotic evil]] | magical-GW = | layers-GW = | layer-number-GW = 66 | location-GW = the [[Abyss]] | refs-GW = <ref name="FC13e-p122-127">{{Cite book/Fiendish Codex I: Hordes of the Abyss|122-127}}</ref> | type-WA = Layer | shape-size-WA = | gravity-WA = | mutability-WA = | element-energy-WA = | alignment-WA = | magical-WA = | layers-WA = | layer-number-WA = 66 | location-WA = the [[Abyss]] | refs-WA = <ref name="MotP4e-p81">{{Cite book/Manual of the Planes 4th edition|81}}</ref><ref name="DN4e-p80">{{Cite book/Demonomicon|80}}</ref> | type-WT = [[Fiendish Plane]] | shape-size-WT = | gravity-WT = | time-WT = | morphic-WT = Alterable (each realm is divinely morphic) | element-energy-WT = | alignment-WT = Mildly chaos-aligned and strongly evil-aligned | magical-WT = | faith-WT = Strong | layers-WT = | layer-number-WT = | location-WT = | refs-WT = <ref name="PGtF-p141">{{Cite book/Player's Guide to Faerûn|141}}</ref><ref name="PGtF-pp149-150">{{Cite book/Player's Guide to Faerûn|149-150}}</ref> | inhabitants = yes | deities = yes | locations = yes | organizations = | settlements = | usethe = yes | useon = }} The '''Demonweb Pits''', also known as '''Lolth's Web''',<ref name="DD-28"/><ref name="OHG-100">{{Cite book/On Hallowed Ground|100}}</ref> was originally the 66{{th}} layer of the [[Abyss]].<ref name="Condemn-p306">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|306}}</ref> By the end of the [[Silence of Lolth]], Lolth had moved her domain in the Demonweb Pits to its own [[plane|planar space]].<ref name="Annih-p311">{{Cite book/Annihilation/Paperback|311}}</ref>
The realm was ruled over by Lolth, the primary drow [[deity]], who resided in a huge [[iron]] fortress that moved under its mistress's will on spider-like legs. Her deific consort [[Selvetarm]] lived with her there until he fell before a wielder of the ''[[Crescent Blade]]''. After that, for a century, every creature who resided in the Demonweb Pits answered solely to Lolth. In the 1480s DR Selvetarm returned to life and to his domain.{{fact}}
==Description== ===Old Demonweb Pits=== When [[Quenthel Baenre]] and her companions visited the Demonweb Pits in the Abyss during the Silence of Lolth in the {{YearlinkName|1372}}, they found the realm unusually empty of souls.<ref name="Condemn-p342">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|342}}</ref> The realm consisted of black emptiness with an acrid smell and giant spider web.<ref name="Condemn-p338-339">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|338-339}}</ref> It was very hot there.<ref name="Condemn-p349">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|349}}</ref> The Pits were covered in corpses of monsters and [[demon]]s lying dead and dying, particularly [[goristro]]s.<ref name="Condemn-p341">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|341}}</ref> Lolth dwelt in a black temple suspended in the web. Her stone face covered the entrance.<ref name="Condemn-p352-353">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|352-353}}</ref>
When Quenthel's expedition returned to the same location in the {{YearlinkName|1373}}, they found the Demonweb Pits abandoned and in ruins.<ref name="Annih-p306">{{Cite book/Annihilation/Paperback|306}}</ref> A [[gate]] guarded by [[abyssal widow]]s led to the new Demonweb Pits.<ref name="Annih-p371">{{Cite book/Annihilation/Paperback|371}}</ref>
===New Demonweb Pits=== The new Demonweb Pits was a plane of rocks with chasms and rocky gorges. There were many pits and craters. The land looked dead. There were giant petrified spiders with webbing over everything from the songspiders.<ref name="Res-p29-31">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|29-31}}</ref> There was a distant red sun during the day<ref name="Res-p54">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|54}}</ref> and eight bright red stars at night.<ref name="Res-p361">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|361}}</ref>
There was a river of souls flowing to Lolth's city, an iron citadel in the Infinite Web.<ref name="Res-p39">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|39}}</ref><ref name="Res-p214">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|214}}</ref> Lolth stood atop a dais in a temple on a pyramid with webs on the walls.<ref name="Res-p316">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|316}}</ref>
There were a number of geographical features on the plane, including the [[Plains of Soulfire]]<ref name="Res-p13">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|13}}</ref> and the [[Pass of the Soulreaver]] at the base of the [[Mountain of Eyes]].<ref name="Res-p189">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|189}}</ref>
The plane was inhabited by [[spider]]s (including [[songspider]]s)<ref name="Res-p29-31">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|29-31}}</ref> and [[chwidencha]].<ref name="Res-p81">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|81}}</ref> The [[Soulreaver]] dwelt in the Pass of the Soulreaver and was a gray spectral form, with a bloated serpentine body containing screaming drow souls.<ref name="Res-p266">{{Cite book/Resurrection/Paperback|266}}</ref>
After the [[Second Sundering]], Lolth returned her realm to the Abyss.<ref name="5e DMG">{{Cite book/Dungeon Master's Guide 5th edition}}</ref>
==Gods and Domains== All drow gods were originally located in the Demonweb Pits and Lolth claimed to be the queen of them all.<ref name="Condemn-p339-340">{{Cite book/Condemnation/Paperback|339-340}}</ref>
* Lolth's son, [[Vhaeraun]], maintained a realm named [[Ellaniath]] where he schemed against his mother almost constantly, an activity Lolth actually encouraged. After Lolth's Silence, Lolth exiled him from the new Demonweb pits.{{fact}}
* Lolth's daughter, [[Eilistraee]], also had a place in the Demonweb pits, but her main realm was in [[Ysgard]] and successively in [[Arvandor]]. However, after the Silence of Lolth, her secondary realm was removed from the Demonweb.{{fact}}
* [[Kiaransalee]] had her own citadel made of bones called [[Thanatos (Abyss)|Thanatos]] in a desolate area of the plane. She grudgingly worked for Lolth as her servant since her own layer of the Abyss was stolen from her by the reincarnated demon prince [[Orcus]]. However with her death due to the [[high magic]] of [[Q'arlynd Melarn]], her dominion crumbled. As of the 1480s, Kiaransalee re-emerged.{{fact}}
* [[Ghaunadaur]] resided at the very bottom of the pits, surrounded by slime and fungus that caused multicolored lights to appear. However, in the {{YearlinkName|1379}}, fed up with the Spider Queen, he removed his dominion to the [[Deep Caverns]].{{fact}}
* [[Selvetarm]] resided with the Spider Queen without maintaining a realm of his own.<ref name="PGtF-pp149-150"/><ref name="DD-36">{{Cite book/Demihuman Deities|36}}</ref>
